It was my second Saturday shift in the café.
I have already learned to do a lot of the work.
That morning it was wonderfully warm outside.
A woman came over to the counter.
"I would like to ask for a ginger beer," she said.
"Of course, just a moment," I answered.
I went over to the large glass fridge behind the counter.
I looked on the third shelf.
The cold bottles of ginger beer were standing there.
I found a bottle and took it out.
The ginger lay like a thick cloud down at the bottom.
I have learned to mix it before I open the bottle.
So I turned the bottle very carefully upside down.
I held it like that for a couple of seconds.
The ginger mixed slowly with the rest of the liquid.
Now the drink looked exactly right.
I turned the bottle around again and placed it on the counter.
"Here you go, that will be thirty-five kroner," I said to her.
She paid, and she has probably enjoyed her cold drink.
